{
  "slug": "ws",
  "name": "Ws",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "ws is a working set manager for Claude Code. Use /ws:map to describe a feature and Claude automatically identifies relevant files across your codebase, adding them to a focused, navigable list. Use /ws:install to set up the ws CLI on any OS. Working sets are branch-scoped and persistent — switch git branches and your context switches with you. Built for AI-assisted coding workflows where you need to track a curated set of files rather than browse your entire project tree.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills**, `install` (Install the ws CLI tool using the recommended method for the current OS), `map` (Find all files relevant to a feature, flow, or area of the codebase and add them to your…).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install ws@claude-community` from `n-filatov/ws`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
